From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:07:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] zink: import a dma-buf short of the TFU readahead

zink allocates an imported dma-buf with the image's memory
requirements. Mesa 26.x's V3DV adds the TFU's 64-byte readahead to the
requirement of every TRANSFER_SRC image (24.0.7's did not), and zink
gives its images that usage, while an exporter that allocated the
image without it does not pad: in DomU on a Raspberry Pi 5 host, a
1920x720 XRGB buffer from a Venus swapchain is 5529600 bytes and
zink's image wants 5529664. The host's V3DV refuses an import bigger
than the dma-buf (device_import_bo), and so does the guest's Venus
for a mappable blob, so agl-compositor on zink took no client buffer
("Error during import, and no known conversion for format XR24"),
measured on 2026-10-17.

When a single-plane image falls short of the dma-buf by no more than
that padding, allocate what the dma-buf holds. The check does not
look at the driver: any driver's import short by up to 64 bytes now
goes through. The image is then bound to less memory than
vkGetImageMemoryRequirements asked for
(VUID-vkBindImageMemory-size-01049), which V3DV does not check at
bind, and a TFU read of the whole image runs up to 64 bytes past the
dma-buf and can raise a V3D MMU error.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_resource.c
@@ -45,6 +45,9 @@
 #include "util/u_memory.h"
 #include "util/u_upload_mgr.h"
 #include "util/os_file.h"
+#ifndef _WIN32
+#include <unistd.h>
+#endif
 #include "frontend/winsys_handle.h"
 
 #if !defined(__APPLE__)
@@ -53,6 +56,11 @@
 
 #if defined(ZINK_USE_DMABUF) && !defined(_WIN32)
 #include "drm-uapi/drm_fourcc.h"
+
+/* how far an imported dma-buf may fall short of the image's memory
+ * requirement: V3DV's TFU readahead padding (V3D_TFU_READAHEAD_SIZE)
+ */
+#define ZINK_IMPORT_PAD_MAX 64
 #else
 /* these won't actually be used */
 #define DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID 0
@@ -1223,6 +1231,23 @@
          goto fail1;
       }
 
+      /* An import cannot be bigger than the dma-buf it comes from, but V3DV
+       * pads a TRANSFER_SRC image by the TFU's 64-byte readahead, which an
+       * exporter allocating the image without that usage (such as a Venus
+       * swapchain) does not, so a tightly sized dma-buf fails to import.
+       * Allocate what the dma-buf holds when a single-plane image falls
+       * short of it by no more than that padding.
+       */
+      if (external == VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_DMA_BUF_BIT_EXT &&
+          obj->plane_count == 1 &&
+          util_format_get_num_planes(templ->format) == 1) {
+         off_t dmabuf_size = lseek(imfi.fd, 0, SEEK_END);
+         lseek(imfi.fd, 0, SEEK_SET);
+         if (dmabuf_size > 0 && (VkDeviceSize)dmabuf_size < reqs.size &&
+             reqs.size - (VkDeviceSize)dmabuf_size <= ZINK_IMPORT_PAD_MAX)
+            reqs.size = dmabuf_size;
+      }
+
       imfi.pNext = mai.pNext;
       mai.pNext = &imfi;
    }
